                        "glosses": [
                            "A cart, often two-wheeled, that can be tilted to empty its contents."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ceaae6c-f36b-47a1-899b-6b5da83ec4c6",
                                "sense_id": "aa88cbd7-ab5d-3f93-ae35-a3d1158d5c3d",
                                "text": "When James' Bay mud flats had become too \"towny\" to be a rubbish heap any more, the little two-wheeled, one-horse dump-carts trundled their loads of garbage to the unmade end of Cook Street and spilled it among the boggy ooze."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0abd006a-ed3a-4d84-b643-5e3763a4be63",
                                "sense_id": "aa88cbd7-ab5d-3f93-ae35-a3d1158d5c3d",
                                "text": "1955, Albert Camus, \"The Minotaur, or the Stop in Oran\" (1939), translated by Justin O'Brien, New York: Vintage, 1991, p. 176,\nFarther on, dump-carts tip their loads over the slopes; and the rocks, suddenly poured seaward, bound and roll into the water, each large lump followed by a scattering of lighter stones."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
